<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/Use%20a%20standard%20bladder%20cuff%20%2812%E2%80%9313%20cm%20wide%20and%2035%20cm%20long%29%20for%20most%20patients%2C%20but%20use%20larger%20and%20smaller%20cuffs%20for%20larger%20%28arm%20circumference%20%3E32%20cm%29%20and%20smaller%20%28arm%20circumference%20%3C26%20cm%29%20arms%2C%20respectively.> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use a standard bladder cuff (12–13 cm wide and 35 cm long) for most patients, but use larger and smaller cuffs for larger (arm circumference >32 cm) and smaller (arm circumference <26 cm) arms, respectively." .
