<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/Lying%20and%20standing%20BP%20measurements%20should%20also%20be%20considered%20in%20subsequent%20visits%20in%20older%20people%2C%20in%20people%20with%20DM%2C%20and%20in%20other%20conditions%20in%20which%20orthostatic%20hypotension%20may%20frequently%20occur.%20Initial%20orthostatic%20hypotension%20may%20occur%20%3C1%20min%20after%20standing%20and%20may%20be%20difficult%20to%20detect%20with%20conventional%20measurement%20techniques.> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/SurfaceForm> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/su_verified_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_table_14/tu_0009> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Lying and standing BP measurements should also be considered in subsequent visits in older people, in people with DM, and in other conditions in which orthostatic hypotension may frequently occur. Initial orthostatic hypotension may occur <1 min after standing and may be difficult to detect with conventional measurement techniques." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/su_verified_1d4ae21bdadbacafa8087e019976dde180c346c5d4626772c2b286528336efac_table_14/e_0004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/ExtractedEntity> .
